    "field": "Decadal climate prediction",
    "problem": "Decadal climate prediction systems exhibit low skill in the tropical Pacific because spurious trends in the wind stress data used for initialization create a shock, which triggers artificial El Ni\u00f1o and La Ni\u00f1a events and degrades the forecast.",
    "method": "We use a sensitivity experiment, initializing decadal hindcasts using only wind stress forcing, to identify that spurious trends in the initialization wind data are the primary cause of low prediction skill and initialization shock in the tropical Pacific.",
    "task": "The task is to identify the cause of low prediction skill in decadal hindcasts for the tropical Pacific, analyzing how spurious trends in initialization wind stress data lead to an \"initialization shock\" that degrades the forecast.",
    "model": [
        "MPI-ESM",
        "CCSM4"
    ],
